# This directory is intentionally empty for now.
#
# It must exist: `Package.swift` declares a `JanelaGitTests` target, and SwiftPM
# fails to resolve if the directory is missing. Git does not track empty
# directories, so this file is what keeps it alive across a clone. Delete it once
# there is a real test file here.
#
# What belongs here (see docs/testing.md):
#
#   - Worktree creation, listing, removal, against REAL repositories via
#     `GitFixture`. We do not mock git: `git worktree add` either works against a
#     real repository or it does not, and a mock would only test our assumptions.
#   - `git worktree list --porcelain -z` parsing, including the awkward cases:
#     paths containing newlines (this is why we use `-z`), detached HEAD, locked
#     worktrees, prunable entries.
#   - `WorktreeRemovalSafety`: uncommitted changes, untracked files, unpushed
#     commits, locks. Each flag needs a test that sets up the condition for real.
#   - `GitRunner` argument construction — no shell, so assert the argv array.
